{220}{}{The mercenary. She hired a gun, not a name. Names cost extra.}
{221}{}{The stock. Not her, and not the experiments. The stock never asks me to hold something while it lights a fuse.}
{222}{}{Pays on time and smiles while she does it. Last month she asked how many toes a man really needs. I count mine every morning now.}
# Trouble: 223 Burke still in the saloon, 224 bomb disarmed, 225 Simms dead, 226 nothing much, 227 bomb rigged.
{223}{}{Man in a suit, up at Moriarty's. Clean shoes. Nobody out here keeps clean shoes unless somebody else does his walking for him.}
{224}{}{Used to be the bomb. Somebody killed it. Now the worst thing in town is in a jar on that shelf, and I'm paid to stand next to it.}
{225}{}{Sheriff got shot in the back in a bar. That's what a badge buys you. I'll keep the shotgun and skip the star.}
{226}{}{Quiet. I don't trust quiet. Quiet is trouble that hasn't picked a door yet.}
{227}{}{The bomb has hummed ever since somebody had the plate off. If it starts to whistle, I'm over the wall and she can keep my last week's pay.}

{230}{}{Yes. It's a big gun. Stand where I can see you and it stays a quiet one.}
{231}{}{Me touch gun?}
